(BUF-37: a fixed-size DESTINATION buffer truncates when full and sets the error flag, under append/copy.)
(expected output:
4
fixed append truncated (errored)
8
ABCDEFGH
)
a buffer called fixdst is 8 bytes in size.
copy "ABCD" to fixdst.
print fixdst's size.
append "EFGHIJKL" to fixdst.
On error print "fixed append truncated (errored)".
print fixdst's size.
print fixdst.
